# Auto Preview Build After Code Changes

When modifying application source code in this repository (C#, XAML, assets used by the app, etc.):

1. After changes compile successfully, **always** run a preview build without asking the user.
2. Default command:

```powershell
dotnet build "NaiwaProxy.csproj" -c Release
```

3. Tell the user the preview path: `bin\Release\net10.0-windows\Nexora.exe`.

4. If build fails because `Nexora.exe` is locked, stop the running process once and retry:

```powershell
Stop-Process -Name Nexora -Force -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue
dotnet build "NaiwaProxy.csproj" -c Release
```

## Full Installer (only when explicitly requested)

Run publish + Inno Setup **only** when the user explicitly asks for an installable package / installer / setup exe:

```powershell
dotnet publish "NaiwaProxy.csproj" -c Release -r win-x64 --self-contained true -p:PublishSingleFile=true -p:IncludeNativeLibrariesForSelfExtract=true -o "publish\win-x64"
& "C:\Program Files\InnoSetup6\ISCC.exe" "installer\NaiwaProxy.iss"
```

Output: `dist/Nexora-Setup-{version}.exe` (read version from `NaiwaProxy.csproj` or `installer/NaiwaProxy.iss`).

## Skip

Skip building only when the user explicitly says not to, or when changes are docs-only / non-buildable and cannot affect the exe.
